      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "National security is indeed an important consideration, and some argue that protecting domestic industries can help mitigate that risk. However, national security encompasses more than just economic self-sufficiency; it often requires robust international alliances and economic interdependence. These relationships can act as a counterbalance to geopolitical pressures. True long-term national stability also includes the ability to participate in a globalized economy, as this brings opportunities for diplomacy, shared advances, and economic benefits that extend beyond immediate self-sufficiency. While a focus on national self-sufficiency might reduce vulnerability in some respects, it is also important to acknowledge that international cooperation and trade can be equally important in creating a more stable and secure global system.",
